error BYN2782: cannot move out of field `items`

  11 │     let a = move bag.items;
     │                  ^^^^^^^^^
     │
  help: its owner keeps it; take it with `.take()`, or copy it with `.copy(to: alloc)`

error BYN2782: cannot move out of an element

  12 │     let b = move lists[0];
     │                  ^^^^^^^^
     │
  help: its owner keeps it; take it with `.take()`, or copy it with `.copy(to: alloc)`

error BYN2782: cannot move out of parameter `plain`

  13 │     let c = move plain;
     │                  ^^^^^
     │
  help: a plain parameter is borrowed from the caller; declare it `move plain` to take ownership

error BYN2782: cannot move out of `ref` parameter `shared`

  14 │     let d = move shared;
     │                  ^^^^^^
     │
  help: the caller still owns it; copy it with `.copy(to: alloc)`

error BYN2782: cannot move out of a fresh value

  15 │     let e = move make();
     │                  ^^^^^^
     │
  help: a fresh value needs no `move`; remove it
